## Statement

A triangle has sides $5$, $7$ and $8$. Show that one of its angles is $60^\circ$ and compute its area.

## Hint

Apply the law of cosines to the angle opposite the side $7$.

## Solution

Let $\theta$ be the angle opposite the side $7$, between the sides $5$ and $8$. The law of cosines gives
$$7^2=5^2+8^2-2\cdot5\cdot8\cos\theta\quad\Longrightarrow\quad49=89-80\cos\theta\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\cos\theta=\frac12.$$
So $\theta=60^\circ$.

The area is $\dfrac12\cdot5\cdot8\cdot\sin60^\circ=20\cdot\dfrac{\sqrt3}2=10\sqrt3$.

Check with Heron's formula: $s=10$ and the area is $\sqrt{10\cdot5\cdot3\cdot2}=\sqrt{300}=10\sqrt3$.
